text:
rachel: Quick doc sync: we need a short deprecation + migration blurb for the v1->v2 page that covers canarying, a safe runtime fallback pattern, and an embeddings note. Keep it minimal (one paragraph + 2 tiny snippets + curl smoke test). Who can own?

tom: I can take this. Plan: 1) one-paragraph guidance (what to expect & recommended approach), 2) TS + Py snippets for graceful fallback, 3) a single-line curl smoke test, 4) a support ticket template, 5) add a tiny GH Action to run the curl test on docs PRs.

priya: Copy notes: emphasise not to swallow auth errors and to track a metric when fallback happens. Also call out vector-dim risk for embeddings clearly.

tom: Draft paragraph: "When migrating from redwood-v1 to redwood-v2, run a canary on a subset of traffic and validate outputs on your eval set. For availability, implement a targeted fallback that only triggers on network/5xx errors; avoid broad exception handling. If your app uses embeddings, verify vector dimensionality before swapping models (re-encode or pin to the compatible model to prevent retrieval regressions)."

tom: Draft TypeScript snippet (very small):
```ts
import { Client } from '@redwood/inference'
const c = new Client()
async function gen(p){
  try{
    return await c.generate({model:'redwood-v2', input:p})
  }catch(e){
    if (e.status && e.status >= 500){
      // emit metric: migration_fallback_total
      return await c.generate({model:'redwood-v1', input:p})
    }
    throw e
  }
}
```

tom: Draft Python snippet:
```py
from redwood import Client
c = Client()
def gen(prompt):
    try:
        return c.generate(model='redwood-v2', input=prompt)
    except Exception as e:
        if getattr(e, 'status', 0) >= 500:
            # send telemetry: migration_fallback_total
            return c.generate(model='redwood-v1', input=prompt)
        raise
```

priya: Nice. Add a one-line curl check we can use in smoke tests:
```
curl -sS -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/generate -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" -d '{"model":"redwood-v2","input":"ping"}' || curl -sS -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/generate -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" -d '{"model":"redwood-v1","input":"ping"}'
```

janet: Please include a short support template we can paste into tickets: "Observed automatic fallback from redwood-v2 to redwood-v1 for request <request_id> at <timestamp>. Attach sample prompt/output and whether embeddings were used. Recommended immediate action: rerun sample against pinned v1 for deterministic comparisons."

docs-bot: Reminder: update redirect map for any relocated examples and add a changelog bullet under docs/migrations/CHANGELOG.md.

support-bot: Alert configured: post to #support if fallback rate > 5/hour for any single customer.

rachel: Good. tom, open the PR with the paragraph, snippets, curl smoke test, GH Action, telemetry note, and support template. I'll review and merge if green.

tom: PR opened: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4781 — includes everything above and a tiny unit smoke action. cc @rachel.

priya: Quick nit: change wording "fallback" to "availability fallback" in the paragraph to be explicit. Also, add bold warning line above embedding example: "Warning: embedding dimension mismatch may break retrieval systems."

rachel: Thanks — small edits look good. Merging after CI passes. I'll monitor support for new tickets tomorrow morning. :rocket:
